{"name":"Ink Blotch","hex":"#00608b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigment (or dye)-based fluid used for writing, printing etc.","A particular type, color or container of this fluid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply ink to; to cover or smear with ink.","To sign (a contract or similar document)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ink"},{"term":"blotch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An uneven patch of color or discoloration.","An irregularly shaped area."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To mark with blotches.","To develop blotches, to become blotchy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blotch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ink","blocks":[{"text":"Ink is a gel, sol, or solution that contains at least one colorant, such as a dye or pigment, and is used to color a surface to produce an image, text, or design. Ink is used for drawing or writing with a pen, brush, reed pen, or quill. Thicker inks, in paste form, are used extensively in letterpress and lithographic printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg/330px-F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ink","wikidata":"Q127418"},{"title":"Stain","blocks":[{"text":"A stain is a discoloration that can be clearly distinguished from the surface, material, or medium it is found upon. They are caused by the chemical or physical interaction of two dissimilar materials. Accidental staining may make materials appear used, degraded or permanently unclean. Intentional staining is used in biochemical research, and for artistic effect, such as in wood staining, rust staining and stained glass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Patternspage.jpg/330px-Patternspage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=th